From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 21:06:13 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 33/79] packaging/runner: the in-model runner's image layers
 and its pinned assets
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The runner image for this build, not built yet.

- Dockerfile, build.sh, check-image.sh: the circuit frontend layer over a serving image (clang-18, lld-18 and
  tf-runner-frontend-check, checked at every boot), ported from the DeepSeek-V4.1 release line. check-image.sh
  switches the runner with the generic TF_RUNNER; the README names the generic knobs.
- assets.release: the archive the runner's circuit and graph bank come from, DeepSeek-V4.1's runner-assets-20261107
  release asset (sha256 b5c40d32…), used where it is rather than re-hosted.
- assets.sha256: exactly the files the layer takes (calc.tfpc and the graph-v7-powmod bank), each at its sha256.
- assets.py: `fetch` downloads the archive, checks its sha256, unpacks plain files only and checks every file
  against the manifest; `check` compares a local directory with it. RUNNER_ASSETS_URL names a mirror.
- assets.Dockerfile, build-assets.sh: the assets over a frontend image; the build fails unless the circuit route
  computes the engine's probe cells.
- test_assets.py: the fetch and the check offline, and the pins.

Ported from the dsv41 release line (s86 7b79ef92d, and the DeepSeek-V4.1 recipe's runner asset scripts).
